<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Solving a continuous compound inequality with three parts</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Solve the following compound inequality:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">
\( \displaystyle {@L@} \le {@a@}x {@sign_b@} {@abs_b@} < {@U@} \)
</p>
<p><i>(Enter the lower limit and upper limit in the boxes provided.)</i></p>

<p>[[input:ans1]] \( \le x < \) [[input:ans2]]</p>

<div><b>Lower limit:</b> [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div>
<div><b>Upper limit:</b> [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><b>Worked Solution:</b></p>
<p>To solve a continuous compound inequality, we isolate \(x\) in the middle. We achieve this by applying the exact same operations to all three parts of the inequality simultaneously.</p>

<p>First, we remove the constant term from the middle by {@op_word@} {@abs_b@} {@prep_word@} all three parts:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">
\( \displaystyle \begin{aligned}
{@L@} {@inv_sign@} {@abs_b@} &\le {@a@}x < {@U@} {@inv_sign@} {@abs_b@} \\
{@L_step1@} &\le {@a@}x < {@U_step1@}
\end{aligned} \)
</p>

<p>Next, we divide all three parts by the coefficient of \(x\), which is \({@a@}\):</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">
\( \displaystyle \begin{aligned}
\frac{{@L_step1@}}{{@a@}} &\le x < \frac{{@U_step1@}}{{@a@}} \\
{@ta1@} &\le x < {@ta2@}
\end{aligned} \)
</p>

<p>Hence, the correct solution for this compound inequality is:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">
\( \displaystyle \boxed{{@ta1@} \le x < {@ta2@}} \)
</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
